# Term equivalences for the colourspace domain — GMEOW authoring source.
#
# No mature, widely-adopted RDF/OWL colourspace ontology exists. ICC profiles are
# binary file formats; CSS Color Module is a rendering spec; ONVIF provides only
# XML namespace strings for colourspace attributes. GMEOW therefore mints its own
# seed ReferenceFrame individuals (sRGB, CMYK) and uses frameSolver to point to
# authoritative procedural specs by reference (Principle 12).
#
# No MappingSet is declared because there are no TermEquivalence entries to
# compile. The gap is documented here as plain comments (Principle 5).

# REFUSED (Principle 5 — no faithful external term):
#   No external ontology provides a rigorous conceptual model of colourspace as
#   a reference system. GMEOW retains colourspace frames as canonical terms
#   without alignment rather than force weak matches.
# REFUSED (Principle 5):
#   gmeow:FrameRealm, gmeow:FrameKind, gmeow:Axis have no colourspace-specific
#   external counterparts.
